<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d11" for="edge" attr.name="type" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d10" for="edge" attr.name="seq" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d9" for="edge" attr.name="notes" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d8" for="edge" attr.name="flow_id" attr.type="long" />
  <key id="d7" for="node" attr.name="notes" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d6" for="node" attr.name="service" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="node" attr.name="name" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="graph" attr.name="graph_usable" attr.type="boolean" />
  <key id="d3" for="graph" attr.name="categories" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d2" for="graph" attr.name="notes" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="graph" attr.name="link" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="graph" attr.name="name" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="directed">
    <node id="0">
      <data key="d5">TWD/CNN Center (Atlanta on-prem)</data>
      <data key="d6">UserCompanyDataStream</data>
      <data key="d7">Techwood / CNN Center site in Atlanta. Linear Ops QCs the master files here and sends them to S3 via Aspera. Receives the cloud playout back over Direct Connect as a unicast signal (X chain, a tertiary path to air). An on-site auto changeover switch selects between Techwood playout, CNN Center playout and cloud playout. The signal is compressed here and brought to the uplink. Evertz CloudBridge bookends the connection on site.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="1">
      <data key="d5">S3</data>
      <data key="d6">S3</data>
      <data key="d7">Stores all master files for all brands. Files arrive via Aspera from Atlanta and are registered in Evertz Mediator before being transferred to EC2.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2">
      <data key="d5">EC2 (Evertz ORT playout)</data>
      <data key="d6">EC2</data>
      <data key="d7">EC2 instances running Evertz ORT software; files are played out using Evertz Playtime. 10 channels per AZ across three AZs in us-east-1 (30 channels). Each channel has a primary and a backup. Instances are supported by Auto Scaling groups. Multi-AZ redundancy targets five-nines availability. Evertz CloudBridge carries the signal from the ORT back to site. Deployed with about 40 CloudFormation YAML templates.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="3">
      <data key="d5">Direct Connect</data>
      <data key="d6">DirectConnect</data>
      <data key="d7">Carries the playout back to on-prem as a unicast signal. Two paths: the X chain to Atlanta (tertiary path to air) and the BCP path to Hudson Yards, New York (8 channels). Evertz CloudBridge runs in AWS, New York and Atlanta to bookend the connection.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="4">
      <data key="d5">Uplinks (NYC / ATL)</data>
      <data key="d6">UserCompanyEdge</data>
      <data key="d7">Satellite uplinks for distribution to affiliates. The Atlanta uplink receives the compressed signal from the Techwood/CNN Center site. The NYC (Hudson Yards) uplink is fed by the BCP path with 8 channels.</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="0" target="1" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">QC'd master files are sent from Atlanta to S3 via Aspera.</data>
      <data key="d10">0</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0" target="4" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">The signal is compressed and brought to the Atlanta uplink for distribution to affiliates.</data>
      <data key="d10">4</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1" target="2" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">Once registered in Evertz Mediator, master files are transferred to the local EC2 instances running Evertz ORT.</data>
      <data key="d10">1</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2" target="3" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">Files are played out with Evertz Playtime; the playout leaves via Direct Connect using Evertz CloudBridge.</data>
      <data key="d10">2</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3" target="0" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">X chain: the playout returns to the Atlanta site as a unicast signal, a tertiary path to air.</data>
      <data key="d10">3</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3" target="4" id="0">
      <data key="d8">1</data>
      <data key="d9">BCP path: Direct Connect to Hudson Yards (NYC), 8 channels, fed to an uplink.</data>
      <data key="d10">0</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <data key="d0">WarnerMedia HBO: Cloud Linear Playout</data>
    <data key="d1">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hMK2NJ-q9nc</data>
    <data key="d2">HBO/WarnerMedia cloud linear playout in AWS us-east-1. It started as a business continuity (BCP) solution and grew to support 30 channels. Master files are stored in S3, played out from EC2 instances running Evertz ORT/Playtime across three AZs, and returned over Direct Connect to on-prem (Atlanta 'X chain' tertiary path, and Hudson Yards NYC for BCP) for uplink to affiliates. Deployed through about 40 CloudFormation YAML templates as a repeatable process. Target is five-nines availability. Future plans: live venue inputs switched with pre-recorded content on the ORT, and in-cloud muxing/compression for direct handoff to an MVPD.</data>
    <data key="d3">Media &amp; Entertainment, Broadcast, Linear Playout, Business Continuity</data>
    <data key="d4">True</data>
  </graph>
</graphml>
